#import "../../../proofs.typ": speech, footnote

== 4. Of Creation

#speech[#smallcaps[Paragraph 1]: In the beginning it pleased God the Father, Son, and Holy Spirit,#footnote[John 1:2–3; Hebrews 1:2; Job 26:13] for the manifestation of the glory of His eternal power,#footnote[Romans 1:20] wisdom, and goodness, to create or make the world, and all things therein, whether visible or invisible, in the space of six days, and all very good.#footnote[Colossians 1:16; Genesis 1:31]]

#speech[#smallcaps[Paragraph 2]: After God had made all other creatures, He created man, male and female,#footnote[Genesis 1:27] with reasonable and immortal souls,#footnote[Genesis 2:7] rendering them fit unto that life to God for which they were created; being made after the image of God, in knowledge, righteousness, and true holiness;#footnote[Ecclesiastes 7:29; Genesis 1; 26] having the law of God written in their hearts,#footnote[Romans 2:14–15] and power to fulfill it, and yet under a possibility of transgressing, being left to the liberty of their own will, which was subject to change.#footnote[Genesis 3:6]]

#speech[#smallcaps[Paragraph 3]: Besides the law written in their hearts, they received a command not to eat of the tree of knowledge of good and evil,#footnote[Genesis 2:17] which while they kept, they were happy in their communion with God, and had dominion over the creatures.#footnote[Genesis 1:26, 28]]
